IMPORT prelude

-- Migration Act 1958 (Commonwealth) -- lawful and unlawful non-citizens (ss 5(1), 13, 14), visas and their kinds (ss 29, 30), spouse
-- and de facto partner (ss 5CB, 5F), the decision on an application (s 65), bridging visas (ss 37, 72, 73), when a visa ceases because
-- another comes into effect (s 82(2), (2AA), (3)), leaving and re-entering Australia on a visa (ss 79, 81(2), 82(5), (6), (8)),
-- allowing a non-citizen to work (ss 245AB, 245AC, 245AG, 486R(5)), and approval of work sponsors and nominations and the sponsorship
-- obligations (s 5(1) "approved work sponsor", ss 140E, 140GB, 140H, 140Q).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 171, compilation date 4 June 2026 ("Includes amendments: Act No. 75, 2025"; register id C2026C00232), as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1958A00062.txt (retrieved 2026-09-22).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0020 in subjects/au/requirements.jsonl: priority 1, raised 3 times by the Western Australian
-- cradle-to-grave life of Daniel (daniel d033, 2025-01-10: Priya's partner visa, temporary then permanent -- "On what basis; what
-- must the relationship show; what bridging visa in between?"; d035, 2027-01-09: London, a resident return visa -- "What does a
-- permanent resident need to leave and return?"; d047, 2032-02-01: a Skills in Demand visa and sponsorship -- "May a foreigner work
-- without a visa; what must a sponsor do; what salary?"). The ledger names ss 29, 65, 140E-140H and 235. SCOPED to those questions
-- first, with the definitions, conditions and exceptions needed to answer them.
--
-- s 235 (the old offence of working without a visa or in breach of a visa condition) is NOT in this compilation: the endnotes record
-- "s 235 ... rep No 1, 2024" (the Migration Amendment (Strengthening Employer Compliance) Act 2024). The Act's answer to d047 is now
-- the employer's offences and civil penalties in ss 245AB and 245AC.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Migration Regulations 1994, which hold every visa subclass (820/801 partner, 155 resident return, 482 Skills in
-- Demand, the bridging visas), their criteria, travel periods, conditions and the salary threshold -- their answers are INPUTS here;
-- valid applications (ss 45-46A); health criteria and character (s 501); cancellation (ss 109-140); the s 82(2A) enforcement-visa
-- rule; ss 245AAA-245AAC (coercion), 245AD (aggravated offences), 245AE-245AEB (referral), 245AF (exclusions) and 245AJ (executive
-- officers); s 245AG(2)(c) and (d) (chattels for transport, premises for sexual services); labour market testing itself (s 140GBA)
-- beyond whether it is satisfied; bars and cancellation of sponsors (ss 140K-140M); s 140HA (the matters the regulations must cover,
-- including "a market salary rate"); detention and removal. The value of a penalty unit is set by the Crimes Act 1914, not this Act.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example encodings. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Migration Act 1958`

§§ `5(1), 13 and 14 -- lawful and unlawful non-citizens`

-- s 5(1): "non-citizen means a person who is not an Australian citizen."
-- s 13(1): "A non-citizen in the migration zone who holds a visa that is in effect is a lawful non-citizen." (2): "An allowed
-- inhabitant of the Protected Zone who is in a protected area in connection with the performance of traditional activities is a
-- lawful non-citizen."
-- s 14(1): "A non-citizen in the migration zone who is not a lawful non-citizen is an unlawful non-citizen."
GIVEN `is an Australian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is in the migration zone` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `holds a visa that is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a Protected Zone inhabitant there for traditional activities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a lawful non-citizen` IF
        (NOT `is an Australian citizen`)
    AND (    (`is in the migration zone` AND `holds a visa that is in effect`)
         OR  `is a Protected Zone inhabitant there for traditional activities`)

GIVEN `is an Australian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is in the migration zone` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `holds a visa that is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a Protected Zone inhabitant there for traditional activities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an unlawful non-citizen` IF
        (NOT `is an Australian citizen`)
    AND `is in the migration zone`
    AND (NOT `is a lawful non-citizen` `is an Australian citizen` `is in the migration zone` `holds a visa that is in effect` `is a Protected Zone inhabitant there for traditional activities`)

§§ `29 and 30 -- visas, permanent and temporary`

-- s 29(1): "the Minister may grant a non-citizen permission, to be known as a visa, to do either or both of the following: (a) travel to
-- and enter Australia; (b) remain in Australia." (3): a visa may be one to travel to and enter during a period and, if the holder does,
-- "(i) remain in it during a prescribed or specified period or indefinitely; and (ii) if the holder leaves Australia during a
-- prescribed or specified period, travel to and re-enter it during a prescribed or specified period."
-- s 30(1): "a visa, to be known as a permanent visa, to remain indefinitely." (2): "a visa, to be known as a temporary visa, to remain:
-- (a) during a specified period; or (b) until a specified event happens; or (c) while the holder has a specified status."
DECLARE `Permission to remain` IS ONE OF
    `indefinitely`
    `during a specified period`
    `until a specified event happens`
    `while the holder has a specified status`

GIVEN `the permission to remain` IS A `Permission to remain`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a permanent visa` IF
    CONSIDER `the permission to remain`
    WHEN `indefinitely` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the permission to remain` IS A `Permission to remain`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a temporary visa` IF
    NOT `is a permanent visa` `the permission to remain`

§§ `5F and 5CB -- spouse and de facto partner`

-- s 5F(2): "persons are in a married relationship if: (a) they are married to each other under a marriage that is valid for the
-- purposes of this Act; and (b) they have a mutual commitment to a shared life as a married couple to the exclusion of all others; and
-- (c) the relationship between them is genuine and continuing; and (d) they: (i) live together; or (ii) do not live separately and
-- apart on a permanent basis." s 12: validity is decided by Part VA of the Marriage Act 1961 (without s 88E) -- an INPUT here.
-- s 5CB(2): "a person is in a de facto relationship with another person if they are not in a married relationship (for the purposes
-- of section 5F) with each other but: (a) they have a mutual commitment to a shared life to the exclusion of all others; and (b) the
-- relationship between them is genuine and continuing; and (c) they: (i) live together; or (ii) do not live separately and apart on a
-- permanent basis; and (d) they are not related by family". (4): related by family = child, other descendant, or a parent in common.
-- ss 5F(3), 5CB(3): the regulations may provide how each condition is determined (none retrieved).
DECLARE `Couple facts` HAS
    `married to each other under a marriage valid for this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a mutual commitment to a shared life to the exclusion of all others` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the relationship is genuine and continuing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `live together` IS A BOOLEAN
    `live separately and apart on a permanent basis` IS A BOOLEAN
    `related by family` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `c` IS A `Couple facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `share a life together under s 5F or 5CB` IF
        `c`'s `a mutual commitment to a shared life to the exclusion of all others`
    AND `c`'s `the relationship is genuine and continuing`
    AND (`c`'s `live together` OR (NOT `c`'s `live separately and apart on a permanent basis`))

GIVEN `c` IS A `Couple facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `are spouses under s 5F` IF
        `c`'s `married to each other under a marriage valid for this Act`
    AND `share a life together under s 5F or 5CB` `c`

GIVEN `c` IS A `Couple facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `are de facto partners under s 5CB` IF
        (NOT `are spouses under s 5F` `c`)
    AND `share a life together under s 5F or 5CB` `c`
    AND (NOT `c`'s `related by family`)

§§ `65 -- decision to grant or refuse to grant a visa`

-- s 65(1): "Subject to sections 84 and 86, after considering a valid application for a visa, the Minister: (a) if satisfied that: (i)
-- the health criteria for it (if any) have been satisfied; and (ii) the other criteria for it prescribed by this Act or the regulations
-- have been satisfied; and (iii) the grant of the visa is not prevented by section 40 ..., 501 ... or any other provision of this Act or
-- of any other law of the Commonwealth; and (iv) any amount of visa application charge payable in relation to the application has been
-- paid; is to grant the visa; or (b) if not so satisfied, is to refuse to grant the visa." Note 1: s 84 allows processing to be
-- suspended; s 86 prevents a grant once a capped number is reached. The criteria for subclasses 820 and 801 are in Schedule 2 of the
-- Regulations, not the Act. Treating ss 84 and 86 as leaving the application undecided is an INFERENCE from "Subject to".
DECLARE `Decision` IS ONE OF
    `grant the visa`
    `refuse to grant the visa`
    `no decision under s 65 yet`

GIVEN `a valid application has been considered` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `processing is suspended under s 84 or capped under s 86` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `satisfied the health criteria are met` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `satisfied the other prescribed criteria are met` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `satisfied no provision prevents the grant` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the visa application charge is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Decision`
DECIDE `the s 65 decision` IS
    IF (NOT `a valid application has been considered`) OR `processing is suspended under s 84 or capped under s 86`
    THEN `no decision under s 65 yet`
    ELSE IF     `satisfied the health criteria are met`
            AND `satisfied the other prescribed criteria are met`
            AND `satisfied no provision prevents the grant`
            AND `the visa application charge is paid`
         THEN `grant the visa`
         ELSE `refuse to grant the visa`

§§ `37, 72 and 73 -- bridging visas`

-- s 37: "There are classes of temporary visas, to be known as bridging visas, to be granted under Subdivision AF."
-- s 72(1): "eligible non-citizen means a non-citizen who: (a) has been immigration cleared; or (b) is in a prescribed class of persons;
-- or (c) the Minister has determined to be an eligible non-citizen." ((c) is confined by (2) to protection-visa applicants detained
-- for more than 6 months.)
-- s 73: "If the Minister is satisfied that an eligible non-citizen satisfies the criteria for a bridging visa as prescribed under
-- subsection 31(3), the Minister may grant a bridging visa permitting the non-citizen to remain in, or to travel to, enter and remain in
-- Australia: (a) during a specified period; or (b) until a specified event happens." "May": a power, not a duty.
-- s 76(1): holding a bridging visa does not prevent an application for, or the grant of, a visa of another class.
GIVEN `has been immigration cleared` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is in a prescribed class of persons` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Minister has determined it under s 72(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an eligible non-citizen under s 72` IF
    `has been immigration cleared` OR `is in a prescribed class of persons` OR `the Minister has determined it under s 72(1)(c)`

GIVEN `is an eligible non-citizen` IS A BOOLEAN, `satisfies the prescribed bridging visa criteria` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may grant a bridging visa under s 73` IF
    `is an eligible non-citizen` AND `satisfies the prescribed bridging visa criteria`

§§ `82(2), (2AA) and (3) -- a visa ceases when another comes into effect`

-- s 5(1): "substantive visa means a visa other than: (a) a bridging visa; or (b) a criminal justice visa; or (c) an enforcement visa."
-- s 82(2): "A substantive visa held by a non-citizen ceases to be in effect if another substantive visa (other than a special purpose
-- visa) for the non-citizen comes into effect." (2AA): neither rule runs between a maritime crew visa and a substantive visa of a class
-- the Minister specifies by legislative instrument (an INPUT). (3): "A bridging visa held by a non-citizen ceases to be in effect if
-- another visa (other than a special purpose visa or a maritime crew visa) for the non-citizen comes into effect."
DECLARE `Visa category` IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary substantive visa`
    `a special purpose visa`
    `a maritime crew visa`
    `a bridging visa`
    `a criminal justice visa`
    `an enforcement visa`

GIVEN `the category` IS A `Visa category`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a substantive visa` IF
    CONSIDER `the category`
    WHEN `a bridging visa` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a criminal justice visa` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an enforcement visa` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the category` IS A `Visa category`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a maritime crew visa` IF
    CONSIDER `the category`
    WHEN `a maritime crew visa` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the category` IS A `Visa category`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a special purpose visa` IF
    CONSIDER `the category`
    WHEN `a special purpose visa` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the held visa` IS A `Visa category`,
      `the new visa` IS A `Visa category`,
      `an s 82(2AA) instrument covers the class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the held visa ceases when the new visa comes into effect` IF
        (    `is a substantive visa` `the held visa`
         AND `is a substantive visa` `the new visa`
         AND (NOT `is a special purpose visa` `the new visa`)
         AND (NOT (    `an s 82(2AA) instrument covers the class`
                   AND (`is a maritime crew visa` `the held visa` OR `is a maritime crew visa` `the new visa`))))
    OR  (    (`the held visa` EQUALS `a bridging visa`)
         AND (NOT `is a special purpose visa` `the new visa`)
         AND (NOT `is a maritime crew visa` `the new visa`))

§§ `79, 81(2) and 82(5), (6), (8) -- leaving and re-entering Australia`

-- s 79: "If the holder of a visa leaves Australia the holder may only re-enter Australia because of the visa if: (a) the visa is
-- permission for the re-entry; and (b) the visa is in effect on re-entry."
-- s 81(2): "A visa to enter Australia within a period is not permission to so enter outside that period."
-- s 82(5): a visa to travel to and enter Australia during a particular period "ceases to be in effect at the end of that period ...
-- unless the holder of the visa: (a) has entered Australia in that period ...; and (b) is in Australia at the end of that period".
-- s 82(6): such a visa "ceases to be in effect if the holder leaves Australia after that period or date."
-- s 82(8): "A visa to remain in, but not re-enter, Australia that is granted to a non-citizen in Australia ceases to be in effect if the
-- holder leaves Australia."
-- The length of a permanent visa's re-entry period, and the resident return visa (subclass 155) that gives a new one, are in the
-- Regulations; the period's end is an INPUT. Dates are written YYYYMMDD.
DECLARE `Travel facts` HAS
    `the visa permits re-entry` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the re-entry period ends` IS A NUMBER
    `the visa was granted in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of departure` IS A NUMBER
    `date of return` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `t` IS A `Travel facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the visa ceases when the holder leaves` IF
        ((NOT `t`'s `the visa permits re-entry`) AND `t`'s `the visa was granted in Australia`)
    OR  (`t`'s `the visa permits re-entry` AND `t`'s `date of departure` > `t`'s `the re-entry period ends`)

GIVEN `t` IS A `Travel facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the holder may re-enter on the visa` IF
        `t`'s `the visa permits re-entry`
    AND (NOT `the visa ceases when the holder leaves` `t`)
    AND `t`'s `date of return` <= `t`'s `the re-entry period ends`

GIVEN `has entered Australia in the period` IS A BOOLEAN, `is in Australia at the end of the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the visa ceases at the end of its entry period under s 82(5)` IF
    NOT (`has entered Australia in the period` AND `is in Australia at the end of the period`)

§§ `245AB, 245AC, 245AG and 486R(5) -- allowing a non-citizen to work`

-- s 245AG(1): "work means any work, whether for reward or otherwise." (2): "a person allows a person to work if, and only if: (a) the
-- first person employs the second person under a contract of service; or (b) the first person engages the second person, other than in
-- a domestic context, under a contract for services; or (ba) the first person participates in an arrangement ... for the performance of
-- work by the second person ...; ... or (e) the prescribed circumstances exist." ((c) and (d) are not modelled.)
GIVEN `employs the worker under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `engages the worker under a contract for services` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in a domestic context` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `participates in an arrangement for the work` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the prescribed circumstances exist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `allows the worker to work under s 245AG` IF
        `employs the worker under a contract of service`
    OR  (`engages the worker under a contract for services` AND (NOT `in a domestic context`))
    OR  `participates in an arrangement for the work`
    OR  `the prescribed circumstances exist`

-- s 245AB(1): contravention if "(a) the first person allows, or continues to allow, another person (the worker) to work; and (b) the
-- worker is an unlawful non-citizen." (2): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the first person takes reasonable steps at reasonable times
-- to verify that the worker is not an unlawful non-citizen", including a prescribed computer system. (3) offence: "Imprisonment for 2
-- years or 360 penalty units, or both"; fault element knowledge or recklessness (4). (5) civil penalty: 240 penalty units.
GIVEN `allows the worker to work` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the worker is an unlawful non-citizen` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took reasonable steps at reasonable times to verify` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `contravenes s 245AB(1)` IF
    `allows the worker to work` AND `the worker is an unlawful non-citizen` AND (NOT `took reasonable steps at reasonable times to verify`)

-- s 245AC(1): contravention if "(a) the first person allows, or continues to allow, another person (the worker) to work; and (b) the
-- worker is a lawful non-citizen; and (c) the worker holds a visa that is subject to a work-related condition; and (d) the worker is in
-- breach of the work-related condition solely because of doing the work referred to in paragraph (a)." (2): the same reasonable-steps
-- exception. Penalties as for s 245AB. s 5(1): "work-related condition means a condition: (a) prohibiting the holder of a visa from
-- working in Australia; or (b) restricting the work that the holder of a visa may do in Australia." The conditions themselves (s 41(2)(b))
-- are in the Regulations.
GIVEN `allows the worker to work` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the worker is a lawful non-citizen` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the visa is subject to a work-related condition` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the worker is in breach solely because of this work` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took reasonable steps at reasonable times to verify` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `contravenes s 245AC(1)` IF
        `allows the worker to work`
    AND `the worker is a lawful non-citizen`
    AND `the visa is subject to a work-related condition`
    AND `the worker is in breach solely because of this work`
    AND (NOT `took reasonable steps at reasonable times to verify`)

-- s 486R(5): the pecuniary penalty "must not be more than: (a) if the person is a body corporate -- 5 times the amount of the pecuniary
-- penalty specified for the civil penalty provision; and (b) otherwise -- the amount ... specified".
GIVEN `the specified civil penalty units` IS A NUMBER, `is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum civil penalty in penalty units` IS
    IF `is a body corporate` THEN 5 * `the specified civil penalty units` ELSE `the specified civil penalty units`

GIVEN `is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum civil penalty under s 245AB(5) or 245AC(5)` IS
    `the maximum civil penalty in penalty units` 240 `is a body corporate`

§§ `5(1), 140E, 140GB, 140H and 140Q -- work sponsors, nominations and sponsorship obligations`

-- s 140E(1): "The Minister must approve a person as a work sponsor in relation to one or more classes prescribed ... if prescribed
-- criteria are satisfied."
-- s 5(1): "approved work sponsor means: (a) a person: (i) who has been approved under section 140E as a work sponsor ...; and (ii) whose
-- approval has not been cancelled under section 140M, or otherwise ceased to have effect under section 140G ...; or (b) a person (other
-- than a Minister) who is a party to a work agreement."
GIVEN `approved under s 140E as a work sponsor` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the approval has been cancelled or has ceased` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a party to a work agreement` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an approved work sponsor` IF
        (`approved under s 140E as a work sponsor` AND (NOT `the approval has been cancelled or has ceased`))
    OR  (`is a party to a work agreement` AND (NOT `is a Minister`))

-- s 140GB(2): "The Minister must approve a person's nomination if: (a) in a case to which section 140GBA applies, unless the person is
-- exempt under section 140GBB or 140GBC -- the labour market testing condition under section 140GBA is satisfied; and (aa) in a case in
-- which the person is liable to pay nomination training contribution charge in relation to the nomination -- the person has paid the
-- charge; and (ab) in any case -- the person is an approved work sponsor; and (b) in any case -- the prescribed criteria are satisfied."
GIVEN `section 140GBA applies` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is exempt under s 140GBB or 140GBC` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the labour market testing condition is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is liable to the nomination training contribution charge` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has paid the charge` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the nominator is an approved work sponsor` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the prescribed criteria are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister must approve the nomination under s 140GB(2)` IF
        ((NOT `section 140GBA applies`) OR `is exempt under s 140GBB or 140GBC` OR `the labour market testing condition is satisfied`)
    AND ((NOT `is liable to the nomination training contribution charge`) OR `has paid the charge`)
    AND `the nominator is an approved work sponsor`
    AND `the prescribed criteria are satisfied`

-- s 140H(1): "A person who is or was an approved sponsor must satisfy the sponsorship obligations prescribed by the regulations." The
-- obligations themselves -- including paying "a market salary rate (however described)" (s 140HA(1)(a)) -- are in the Regulations.
-- s 140Q(1): failing to satisfy a sponsorship obligation the regulations impose: "Civil penalty: (a) if the person is an approved work
-- sponsor -- 240 penalty units; or (b) in any other case -- 60 penalty units." s 486R(5) multiplies by 5 for a body corporate.
GIVEN `is an approved work sponsor now` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum civil penalty under s 140Q(1)` IS
    IF `is an approved work sponsor now`
    THEN `the maximum civil penalty in penalty units` 240 `is a body corporate`
    ELSE `the maximum civil penalty in penalty units` 60 `is a body corporate`
